<title>BELGIUM: Belgian CERA Group cons net profit up 69.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Belgian CERA Group cons net profit up 69.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996 earnings</p>
<p>(billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit			 2.863  vs 1.685</p>
<p>    Cons pre-tax profit		   3.015  vs 1.767</p>
<p>NOTE: The CERA Group's CERA Bank is Belgium's sixth largest bank.  </p>
<p>    Depreciation, writeoffs, provisions     3.516 vs     2.849</p>
<p>    Taxes					     1.087 vs     0.471</p>
<p>    Private sector credits		    418     vs   383</p>
<p>    Public sector credits		     326     vs   283</p>
<p>    Credits to credit institutions	  304     vs   244</p>
<p>    Customer deposits			   791     vs   722</p>
<p>    Balances of credit institutions	 350     vs   276</p>
<p>    Total assets				1,241     vs 1,094</p>
</text>
